        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 16: Deploying Applications with Kubernetes\nP\u00e1ginas: 594-653\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (594)\n\u2022 Introducing Kubernetes  (595)\n  \u2022 Understanding the Kubernetes architecture  (596)\n  \u2022 Introducing the Kubernetes object model  (596)\n  \u2022 The anatomy of a Kubernetes cluster  (599)\n\u2022 Installing and configuring Kubernetes  (602)\n  \u2022 Installing Kubernetes on a desktop  (602)\n  \u2022 Installing Kubernetes on VMs  (604)\n\u2022 Working with Kubernetes  (622)\n  \u2022 Using kubectl  (622)\n  \u2022 Deploying applications  (630)\n  \u2022 Running Kubernetes in the cloud  (650)\n\u2022 Summary  (651)\n\u2022 Questions  (651)\n\u2022 Further reading  (652)\n16\nDeploying Applications\nwith Kubernetes\nWhether you are a seasoned system administrator managing containerized applications or a DevOps\nengineer automating app orchestration workflows, Kubernetes could be your platform of choice. This\nchapter will introduce you to Kubernetes and will guide you through the basic process of building\nand configuring a Kubernetes cluster . We\u2019ll use Kubernetes to run and scale a simple application in\na secure and highly available environment. You will also learn how to interact with Kubernetes using\nthe command-line interface ( CLI ).\nBy the end of this chapter, you\u2019ll learn how to install, configure, and manage a Kubernetes cluster\non-premises. We\u2019ll also show you how to deploy and scale an application using Kubernetes.\nHere\u2019s a brief outline of the topics we will cover in this chapter:\n\u2022I Introducing Kubernetes architecture and the API object model\n\u2022I Installing and configuring Kubernetes\n\u2022 Working with Kubernetes using the kubectl command-line tool and deploying applications",
